SUMMARY:Tot Shabbat
DESCRIPTION:Come together with Shoresh and Ner Tamid families for an evening of Shabbat fun\, food\, & friendship. We’ll begin with a brief\, clergy-led Tot Shabbat service\, followed by a community potluck Shabbat dinner. All are welcome! \nWe kindly ask each family to bring a dairy/parve\, nut-free side dish or dessert to share. TNT will provide the main entrees. \nLooking forward to celebrating Shabbat with you! \nREGISTER HERE!
URL:https://nertamid.org/event/tot-shabbat-7-2/
CATEGORIES:Worship
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Nertamid": "https://nertamid.org/event/erev-shabbat-service-4-6/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:nertamid
X-SOURCE:Temple Ner Tamid
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260417T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260417T193000
DTSTAMP:20260417T230719
CREATED:20260413T184024Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260413T184025Z
UID:10000613-1776450600-1776454200@nertamid.org
SUMMARY:Erev Shabbat Service with Kabbalat Shabbat Band
DESCRIPTION:Erev Shabbat services begin on Friday at 6:30pm. These services are especially musical\, often with a band of congregants accompanying the Cantor. Usually around an hour\, these services are filled with a lot of spirit. It’s not uncommon to see people dancing in their seat or hear the whole congregation clapping their hands. Friday night is intergenerational. Glance around and see senior citizens sitting beside religious school families both getting something out of the services.  \nIn the summer months\, services are led by members of the congregation with support from our clergy.\nJoin us most weeks from anywhere for Erev Shabbat Services through Zoom or our YouTube Livestream.
URL:https://nertamid.org/event/erev-shabbat-service-4-6/
CATEGORIES:Worship
END:VEVENT
