CATEGORIES:Arts
DESCRIPTION:The Department of Art & Design presents the Spring 2026 Art Fo
 rum series. Art Forum is a speaker series featuring artists\, designers\,
  art historians\, curators\, and art critics from around the world presen
 ting their work and ideas in an open forum.  \n \nThe final speaker in th
 is engaging series is curator and artist Max Warsh\, director of the Dr. 
 M. T. Geoffrey Yeh Art Gallery at St. John’s University. He will share in
 sights into his curatorial practice and artistic work.\n \nMax Warsh is a
 n artist and curator whose work begins by photographing cast ornamentatio
 n\, tile\, blocks\, and brickwork on building facades\, then printing the
 se images in bulk to use as studio material. He restructures visually rep
 etitive architectural imagery and combines it with paint to create compos
 itions that reflect the production and experience of architecture. The Dr
 . M. T. Geoffrey Yeh Art Gallery is a public exhibition space that partne
 rs with contemporary artists to create dynamic learning opportunities for
  the university and surrounding community.\n \n📅 Art Forum\nMonday\, 4/2
 0/26  5:20pm-7pm\nCalcia Hall\, Room 140\nFree and open to the public \n 
 \n\nHosted by: Art and Design\n\nAdditional Information can be found at: 
 https://montclair.campuslabs.com/engage/event/12432752
DTEND:20260420T230000Z
DTSTAMP:20260418T030714Z
DTSTART:20260420T212000Z
GEO:40.859750;-74.199750
LOCATION:Calcia 140\, Calcia Hall
SEQUENCE:0
